- Target dir: `$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target`

## Provenance

W44-148 (commit `2a303428`) raised variant Z `dct32x32` 1.20 → 1.24 across all 3
variant Z tables (default Z + HC + LC) after broader-corpus measurement showed
1.20 over-fires DCT32X32 (W44-147 audit). The 27-cell W44-148 bisect found 1.24
was Pareto-optimal among {1.20, 1.24, 1.28, 1.30, 1.34}.

W44-153 (`1a988fc8`) full-ledger refresh (591 cells) found 6 cells flipped
FIXED→OPEN at the W44-148 boundary, ALL PARETO SSIM2 WINS (bytes grew past
+3% wedge but SSIM2 IMPROVED +0.07 to +0.24 per cell). These 6 cells were
NOT in the W44-148 27-cell bisect coverage:

* 1420710 e5 d=6 — W44-148 bisect was e6/e7/e8/e9 only
* 1531677 e5/e6 d=6 — W44-148 PROTECT_W99 was at d=5 only
* 1531677 e7 d=5 — W44-148 PROTECT_W99 was e5/e6/e9
* 1531677 e8 d=5 — W44-148 DEFICIT_LC was e7/e8 d=5/6; e8 d=5 was HC class
* 1531677 e9 d=5 — same gap

W44-154 (this chunk) MICRO-bisects {1.22, 1.23} between W44-148's 1.24 and
pre-W44-148 1.20 to find a value that closes ≥4 of the 6 newly-flipped cells
while preserving ≥80% of W44-148's SSIM2 wins on the 1418519 d=5 cluster
(W44-148/W44-152 +0.614 mean).

